 "interpretation": "The /v1/conversations contract holds end to end: containers round-trip through create/get/update/delete with honest 404 tombstones; items append in order with unique digest ids across every append (seed, route, response-turn), through page cursors in both directions, under parallel writes, and across a state-dir restart via conversations.jsonl. Response turns bound by ``conversation`` accumulate input+output items under store=false too; the anchor is exclusive with previous_response_id, refuses in batch lines, and a mid-flight delete fails the queued turn without resurrecting the container. Tenancy is scope-based (read keys GET, write keys mutate) \u2014 the container is shared workspace state, key-agnostic like the retrieval index. Every refusal lands in the wire error envelope. The SDK twin matches.",
